    //- ┅┅┅ `$filesWatching` — Files Watching ┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅┅
    +Heading--YDF({
      level: 2,
      innerHTML: localizedSectioning.filesWatching.$heading,
      HTML_ID: localizedSectioning.filesWatching.$anchor
    }).Article-Heading2

    +PropertyMetadata--YDF_DK($projectBuildingCommonSettingsSpecification.$filesWatching)

    p.Article-Paragraph
      | For project rebuilding as well as automatic reloading of the browser page in
      |   #[+Term--YDID incremental building modes], it is #[+Keyword--YDID necessary] to watch the state of files and
      |   directories.
      | #[+Keyphrase--YDID By default], all files and directories
      |
      +Keyphrase--YDID.
        below the directory containing the #[+ImportantEntity--YDID YDA] configuration file are watched, #[+Keyword--YDID except]:

    ul.Article-UnorderedList

      li Files and directories whose names start with a dot

      li The following files:
        ul.Article-UnorderedList
          each fileName in $$YamatoDaiwaAutomationAPI.FilesWatchingRestrictions.relativePathsOfExcludeFiles
            li= fileName

      li The following directories:
        ul.Article-UnorderedList
          each directoryName in $$YamatoDaiwaAutomationAPI.FilesWatchingRestrictions.relativePathsOfExcludeDirectories
            li= directoryName

    p.Article-Paragraph.
      In addition to this, all files (or at least most of them) to whose state changes #[+ImportantEntity--YDID YDA]
        should&nbsp;not react in any way should be excluded.
      This can be done either for both #[+Term--YDID incremental building modes] or for one of them; moreover, depending
        on the #[+Term--YDID building mode], it makes sense to exclude from watching the #[+Keyword--YDID output] files
        for other #[+Term--YDID building modes].


    //- ╍╍╍ `excludeFilesWithPathsRelativeToProjectRootDirectory` — Relative Paths of Excluded Files ╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍
    +Heading--YDF({
      level: 3,
